    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u give me a quick comparison between signalized intersections and roundabouts? mostly looking at how they handle peak hour throughput and things like queueing delays and system friction.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Roundabouts generally excel in handling peak hour throughput by maintaining continuous flow, unlike signalized intersections that force stop-and-go patterns. This continuous movement significantly reduces system friction, as drivers rarely experience the complete stop of a traffic light. Queueing delays at roundabouts are often less severe, as traffic merges and yields rather than stops completely at an intersection. Overall, roundabouts prioritize smoother movement and higher capacity under heavy load compared to traditional signaling.",
      "source": "target",
