      "content": "right, so it's mostly just human error or saturation. but sometimes it feels like there's just this random, chaotic element that messes up the flow even when the numbers look okay on paper. how do urban planners account for that kind of unpredictable \"noise\" in a system?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
